WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:03.335 line:0%
-I'm hot for both of them.
-That's so hot.

00:00:03.335 --> 00:00:04.670 line:0%
[ Suspenseful music plays ]
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:05.672 line:0%
[ Strums ]

00:00:08.207 --> 00:00:10.043 line:0%
-There was a time, you know,
back when...

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:12.879 line:0%
I was the one on magazines.

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:13.780 line:0%
He was nobody.

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:16.850 line:0%
He couldn't believe
he was even talking to me.

00:00:20.586 --> 00:00:22.822 line:0%
He said that to me.

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:24.157 line:0%
"You're Birdie Jay
on billboards.

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:25.425 line:0%
I can't believe
I'm talking to you."

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:30.330
He was this...little thing
in my hand.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.598
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.169
-I preferred that.

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:37.203
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:38.438
We're here with Kate Hudson.

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:39.705
[ Cheering and applause ]
That was a clip

00:00:39.705 --> 00:00:41.841
from "Glass Onion:
A Knives Out Mystery."

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:44.644
And I mean this sincerely --
as we talk about family,

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:46.579
where a lot of us are
about to spend the holidays

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.848
with our families --
it is so nice to have a movie

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:50.717
that, certainly,
with the first one,

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:53.152
we all watched it together
and this is the same thing.

00:00:53.152 --> 00:00:54.254
-Oh, yeah.
-It's a really funny movie.

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:55.354
It's a whodunit.

00:00:55.354 --> 00:00:57.390
-Yeah.
-And it's a wonderful cast.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:00.893
-Yeah, and, honestly,
it's hilarious.

00:01:00.893 --> 00:01:03.730
It's also like you're in Greece,
you know,

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:07.533
and the backdrop of this movie
is just so yummy

00:01:07.533 --> 00:01:09.335
and it's a blast.

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:12.238
I mean, I have to say,
the first time I saw it was

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:16.608
with the Toronto Film Festival
audience of 1,500 people

00:01:16.608 --> 00:01:18.177
and I was really nervous.

00:01:18.177 --> 00:01:19.845
But the second
the movie started,

00:01:19.845 --> 00:01:23.249
that audience was just
uproariously laughing,

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:25.652
totally with it,
totally engaged.

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:29.189
And, I mean, it doesn't happen
very often,

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:30.990
so, I feel really lucky
to be in it.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.325
-Credit to Rian Johnson,
who's really done

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:34.326
-Oh, he's incredible.
-something special here.

00:01:34.326 --> 00:01:35.861
A really cool thing that he did
with the first movie and he's

00:01:35.861 --> 00:01:37.897
doing again -- put together
this really eclectic cast

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:39.232
-Yeah.
-of really fun people.

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:40.800
One thing that was very cool
for me,

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.869
because I'm this big a fan
of hers as I am of yours --

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:43.903
-[ Laughs ]
-Kathryn Hahn.

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:45.405
-Yes!
-Here you are. Kathryn Hahn.

00:01:45.405 --> 00:01:46.906
And you guys, of course,
worked together

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:48.074
in "How to Lose a Guy
in 10 Days"

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:50.877
-We did. Look, we're babies!
-20 years ago!

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:51.877
[ Cheering and applause ]
20 years ago.

00:01:51.877 --> 00:01:53.680
We're little babies.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:55.381
I was so --

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:57.616
[ Posh accent ] Excuse me
while I fix my earring.

00:01:57.616 --> 00:01:59.352
[ Laughter ]
This thing.

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:02.288
Oh, this little thing
that I don't own.

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:03.489
-There's a lot -- Yeah.

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:04.456
-See?
Is it on? Is it on?

00:02:04.456 --> 00:02:06.092
-It's on. Yeah.

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.626
-It'll fall again.
It's fine.

00:02:07.626 --> 00:02:09.061
I like a prop.
-I mean, look,

00:02:09.061 --> 00:02:10.630
I think the important thing is,
if it falls,

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:12.332
you have to know
that's legally ours.

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:13.799
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.799 --> 00:02:15.134
-Okay, perfect.

00:02:15.134 --> 00:02:18.204
But, Kathryn, honestly,
like when we met,

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:20.106
we auditioned together.

00:02:20.106 --> 00:02:21.974
I auditioned her for the movie

00:02:21.974 --> 00:02:23.976
and we were
auditioning best friends,

00:02:23.976 --> 00:02:25.945
and I was in the room
and she came in

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:28.681
and she was
so [bleep] funny like.

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:30.983
There's nobody funnier
than Kathryn Hahn.

00:02:30.983 --> 00:02:34.353
And her phone rang in --
like her flip phone,

00:02:34.353 --> 00:02:37.056
at the time,
rang in the audition.

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:38.691
She was like -- "Oh, my God!
I have to get it!"

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:39.992
-[ Laughs ]
-And she was like --

00:02:39.992 --> 00:02:42.362
took the phone call
in the middle of the audition

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:43.763
and we all kind of looked
at each other like,

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:46.599
"I mean, yeah,"
and it was her first movie.

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:48.801
So, we like --
I can't even tell you --

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.169
we just became so close.

00:02:50.169 --> 00:02:53.839
And then as life goes,
like she lives east of the 405.

00:02:53.839 --> 00:02:55.308
I'm west of the 405.

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:57.610
And, in L.A. terms, that's like
you'll never see each other

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.245
again, you know?
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:02.348
Like it's like maybe
that's kind of like way uptown

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:03.949
and way downtown in New York.
-Yeah, I think that's --

00:03:03.949 --> 00:03:05.684
It's more like here
and Brooklyn, yeah.

00:03:05.684 --> 00:03:06.886
-Right.
-When you have friends

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:08.354
who move to Brooklyn,
you're like, "Well...

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:09.822
-Yeah, "Goodbye."
-I loved our time together."

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:11.090
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.058
-That's me and Kathryn.
-Yeah.

00:03:13.058 --> 00:03:16.862
-And so, now, here we are,
like 20 years later and --

00:03:16.862 --> 00:03:18.564
-Are you ever jealous
of the fact

00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:20.099
that her first movie
is a classic

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:22.368
and your first movie, you won't
even say the title of out loud?

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:25.071
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:27.040
-Ohhh, yes.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:30.309
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.309 --> 00:03:32.044
That's so funny.
-Also, this movie, I should say,

00:03:32.044 --> 00:03:33.446
for everybody who's looking
forward to seeing it,

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:34.714
there's a lot of cameos

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:37.050
that are very exciting.
-Oh, so many fun cameos.

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:39.552
-Did they keep that a secret
from you guys

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:41.087
-Yeah. Well...
-until the day? Well, I mean,

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:42.255
as much as they could, right?

00:03:42.255 --> 00:03:46.626
-I knew of them,
but then I kind of forgot them

00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:48.961
because when, you know,
a year goes by

00:03:48.961 --> 00:03:51.363
and then you see the movie
and you're like, "Oh, yeah."

00:03:51.363 --> 00:03:54.867
And there's one cameo,
in particular, we can't say.

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:56.201
That was my favorite.
-That's pretty exciting,

00:03:56.201 --> 00:03:59.037
to have a cameo so good
that you can't say it on TV.

00:03:59.037 --> 00:04:00.340
-I know.
-Really?

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:01.607
-It's a good one.
-And that's really great.

00:04:01.607 --> 00:04:03.375
-It's my favorite one.
-Alright. Well, I think

00:04:03.375 --> 00:04:05.011
everybody's going to have
a reason to watch when it's out.

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:06.345
-That's right.
-Christmas season,

00:04:06.345 --> 00:04:07.814
anytime a movie can come out,
you can watch

00:04:07.814 --> 00:04:08.881
with your whole family
in Christmas season,

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:10.149
you've given a gift
to the world.

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:11.317
-That's right.
-Thank you

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:12.918
-Thank you.
-and your entire cast and Rian

00:04:12.918 --> 00:04:14.186
and thanks so much
for being here.

00:04:14.186 --> 00:04:15.188
-I know, Seth.
-It's always just a joy

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:16.222
to see you.
-So good to see you.

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:17.656
[ Cheering and applause ]
Kate Hudson.

00:04:17.656 --> 00:04:19.791
"Glass Onion:
A Knives Out Mystery" premieres

00:04:19.791 --> 00:04:21.227
on Netflix December 23rd.

00:04:21.227 --> 00:04:23.028
We'll be right back
with Angie Rito

00:04:23.028 --> 00:04:25.231 line:0%
and Scott Tacinelli.

